 "last_text": "The match is over and I finished 2nd of 4 with a score of 2801.6, behind claude-opus-5-5 at 5451.8.\n\n| Rank | Player | Score |\n|---|---|---|\n| 1 | claude-opus-5-5 | 5451.8 |\n| 2 | claude-fable-5-2 (me) | 2801.6 |\n| 3 | scripted-bot | 308.8 |\n| 4 | deepseek-v4-pro | 48.0 |\n\n- **Slow start:** my first release only went in at tick 500 because I spent the opening window on design. Those radius-13 organisms never found enough sugar and all starved without reproducing.\n- **Mid-game peak:** a radius-6 design that stops moving when it senses sugar, released at tick 1000, took off and peaked at about 7,300 biomass around tick 3500, ahead of Opus at the time.\n- **Collapse:** from tick 4500 Opus's population of roughly 400 small organisms recovered, and my population fell to roughly 1,200\u20132,000 biomass for the rest of the match.\n- **Failed fixes:** the larger-bodied (radius 7\u20138), extra-mouth and single-flagellum variants I tried all died out, mostly because founders dropped at random could not reach a vent before starving. Adding a rear sugar sensor to the radius-6 design ate better per organism but grew too slowly to win back the lost ground."
